  "regressions": 2,
  "scope": "Whole Federer 3.2.29, pp. 267\u2013268: a subset W of R^n is countably (H^m,m) rectifiable if and only if a countable family of m-dimensional class-one submanifolds contains H^m almost all of W. Both directions hold for all natural dimensions and arbitrary sets W, with no measurability, finite-mass or dimension-bound premise.",
  "proof_route": "Independent countable manifold-family laws precede proved existence. Actual global Lipschitz growth and 3.1.16 give a global C1 approximant with small disagreement. Actual full-rank constant-rank charts and a countable base cover its regular image by submanifolds. Countable finite-measure open Lipschitz neighborhoods, opaque same-bound extensions, actual differential locality and Borel critical supersets give critical-image nullity from 3.2.3. The valid remainder containment and countably many tolerances tending to zero give the global image almost cover. Same-bound extensions of original partial parametrizations, countable unions and the given null remainder give arbitrary-source coverage. For the reverse direction use countable compact chart covers and rectifiability of compact submanifold subsets. Degree zero uses countable singleton manifolds separately.",
  "source_correction_and_conventions": "The p. 268 display equating the uncovered image with the union of two error images is used through its valid containment. Error images can overlap the covered image; no disjointness is assumed. This local set-theoretic correction is absent from the working erratum and does not alter the theorem statement. Punctured growth is used only in positive source dimension; H^0 atoms remain positive.",
  "both_directions": true,
  "arbitrary_sources": true,
  "all_natural_dimensions": true,
  "no_source_measurability_or_finite_mass": true,
  "actual_critical_image_nullity": true,
